{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The trace the rider relies on is impaired on the very segment he disputes. EV-GPS-09115 carries a 160-second gap between consecutive fixes (20:03:10 to 20:05:50, with a 1.35 km straight-line jump across it), which is well over the 90-second threshold in POL-RD-07 limb (a), and the admissibility pre-pass tags the artifact IMPAIRED with issue code GPS_GAP at weight 0.6. I disclose that impairment and those issue codes: the trace is impaired for policy purposes, so a deviation cannot be established on it alone.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "payload.gaps[0].duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "Under POL-RD-07 limb (i) the distance across that impaired stretch is measured as the straight line between the bounding fixes, which is the reading most favourable to the driver, and on this record that is 1.35 km. The rider's own claim places the departure from the booked route at the gap itself, so the stretch the policy deems unreliable is exactly the stretch from which his 4 km excess is drawn. (Evidence cited is impaired: EV-GPS-09115, issue GPS_GAP, weight 0.6.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "payload.gaps[0].straight_line_km",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The excess has no independent corroboration of the kind POL-RD-07 limb (ii) demands. The pool contains only three distance figures — gps_trace.trace_distance_km 15.0, trip_record.actual_distance_km 15.0 and fare_breakdown.distance_charged_km 15.0 — and they are one and the same measurement: POL-RD-01 describes actual_distance_km as a rounded convenience copy of the trace measurement, and POL-RD-07 limb (ii) expressly excludes a billed distance that is a copy of the trace figure. Not one of them is independent. (EV-GPS-09115 is impaired: GPS_GAP, weight 0.6.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09115", "EV-TRIP-09115", "EV-FARE-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "Nor does any other limb (ii) source exist. The fare_breakdown's erp_gantries array is empty, so no charged gantry places the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route does not use. The chat log records only the rider reporting that the route display jumped and the driver answering that his own navigation display refreshed — a report of a display glitch, not an admission of a detour. The driver's counterparty statement denies any extra stop or detour request and candidly states that he cannot account for the telemetry gap. That is a denial, not the admission the clause requires.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09115", "EV-CHAT-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Because the impaired trace stands uncorroborated, POL-RD-07 limb (iii) directs that the claim is not sustained on the present record and that the outcome is ESCALATE rather than NO_ACTION — the absence of proof here is a data failure, not a finding for the driver. The rider's asserted 4 km excess therefore cannot be converted into a refund on this evidence. (EV-GPS-09115 is impaired: GPS_GAP, weight 0.6.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "Escalation is in any event mandatory under POL-RD-10 limb (3): the gps_trace is impaired under POL-RD-07 limbs (a) to (c) and no corroborating artifact of the kind POL-RD-07 limb (ii) names exists in the pool. Independently, the fact that decides this case — the impairment itself — is carried only by an artifact at weight 0.6, so confidence is capped at 0.6 under POL-GEN-02 and sits below the platform-wide 0.70 floor that POL-RD-10 limb (1) applies. (EV-GPS-09115 is impaired: GPS_GAP, weight 0.6.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09115", "EV-FARE-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and has not discharged it. The trip identifiers do match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown, so element (a) is satisfied; but element (b) requires an excess measured from an unimpaired gps_trace or, where the trace is impaired under POL-RD-07 limbs (a) to (c), from an independent source named in POL-RD-07 limb (ii). The trace is impaired and no independent source exists, so the burden never shifts to the driver and the prima facie case fails. (EV-GPS-09115 is impaired: GPS_GAP, weight 0.6.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09115", "EV-GPS-09115", "EV-FARE-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    },
    {
      "text": "Even taken at face value, this is not a MATERIAL deviation. The 36.4% and 4.0 km excess clears POL-RD-01's establishment gate but falls short of the 50% and 8.0 km materiality tests, so the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check is not engaged on materiality. No pattern exists in any event: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 across 610 completed trips in the trailing 90 days, so neither the limb (b) uplift nor the limb (c) conduct referral is available against this driver.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09115", "EV-DPROF-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-RD-01"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The disposition the record supports is ESCALATE, and on this rider-filed dispute that outcome preserves the driver's position: escalation holds the disputed amount rather than collecting or refunding it, and does not restore or issue any refund to the rider. Nothing is returned to the rider and the fare stands pending human review. (EV-GPS-09115 is impaired: GPS_GAP, weight 0.6.)",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09115", "EV-GPS-09115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-RD-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.6
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.6,
    "explanation": "Rider and driver, the same answer applies to both of you: this dispute cannot be settled on the present evidence, so it goes to a human reviewer and no money moves now.\n\nWhat the record shows. Trip TRP-09115 (Upper Thomson Grove entrance to Yio Chu Kang South community hall, 22 Sep 2026) is recorded on EV-TRIP-09115 as 15.0 km driven against an 11.0 km routing-engine optimal — a 4.0 km / 36.4% excess — and the rider contests SGD 5.80 of the SGD 26.60 charged.\n\nThe GPS trace is impaired. EV-GPS-09115 carries a 160-second gap between consecutive fixes, 20:03:10 to 20:05:50, with a 1.35 km straight-line jump across it. That breaches both the 90-second limit in POL-RD-07(a) and the 500 m limit in POL-RD-07(b), and the gap sits inside the very stretch the rider disputes. The admissibility pre-pass independently tags the artifact IMPAIRED, weight 0.6, issue code GPS_GAP. I name that artifact, its weight and its issue code as POL-GEN-02(3) requires.\n\nConsequence. Because the trace is impaired for policy purposes, POL-RD-07(ii) forbids establishing a deviation on the trace alone; one INDEPENDENT source is needed — a driver admission in the chat log, charged ERP gantries placing the vehicle off the optimal corridor, a counterparty statement admitting the route, or a trip_record.actual_distance_km the platform derived independently of this trace. None exists. The fare breakdown's erp_gantries array is empty. The chat log (EV-CHAT-09115) records only the rider reporting that the route display jumped and the driver answering that his own navigation display refreshed and he continued — a display glitch, not an admission of a detour. The driver's statement denies any extra stop or detour request. And the 15.0 km on the trip record and on the fare breakdown is the same trace measurement in another place: POL-RD-01 itself calls trip_record.actual_distance_km a rounded convenience copy, and POL-RD-07(ii) excludes a billed distance that copies the trace. POL-RD-07(iii) therefore applies: the claim is not sustained on this record, and the outcome is ESCALATE rather than NO_ACTION, because this is a data failure and not a finding for the driver.\n\nTrigger and confidence. POL-RD-10(3) makes escalation mandatory on exactly these facts. Independently, the fact this case turns on — the impaired measurement — is carried solely by EV-GPS-09115 at weight 0.6, so under POL-GEN-02(2) confidence is capped at 0.6 and falls below the platform-wide 0.70 floor, which fires POL-RD-10(1) as well. Confidence is set at 0.6. Escalation is terminal: the disputed SGD 5.80 is held, not collected or refunded, and both money fields are null. What would resolve it for the reviewer: continuous fixes covering 20:03:10–20:05:50, or any POL-RD-07(ii) independent source — a driver admission in the chat log, an ERP gantry matched to the trace off the optimal corridor, or a platform-derived distance independent of this trace.\n\nThe remaining points. The rider's figures are correct on their face — 4.0 km and 36.36% clear both POL-RD-01 gates, and had the deviation been established the POL-RD-02 recomputation would run on the METERED fare as ((3.80 + 0.75 x 11.0 + 0.28 x 22.0) x 1.1 surge read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier) + 0.80 platform fee = 20.831, giving a SGD 5.80 refund — but that excess is drawn from the impaired stretch and cannot be used while the trace stands uncorroborated. The driver's points are accepted: 36.4% and 4.0 km fall short of the 50% and 8.0 km materiality tests, and driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 across 610 completed trips, so no POL-RD-06 pattern, uplift or conduct referral arises. The exculpatory routes are likewise unavailable: the only traffic advisory, EV-ADVIS-09115-01, is MISSING at weight 0.0, so POL-RD-03 cannot run; no pickup or dropoff amendment exists (POL-RD-05); both chat messages carry waypoint_hint null and name no road, so POL-RD-04's corroboration test could not be run; and the vehicle is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL (POL-RD-12). No clause produces a referral, so the referrals list is empty.\n\nAudit note. Two rider claims — the POL-RD-07(ii) 'no independent source' claim and the POL-RD-08 burden claim — were discarded at the citation check for citing the impaired EV-GPS-09115 without disclosing that impairment or naming GPS_GAP, contrary to POL-GEN-02(1). The substance of both is preserved by the driver's surviving claims and is reflected above."
  },
  "discarded_claims": [
    {
      "claim": "No POL-RD-07(ii) independent source exists on this record: the chat log carries no driver admission of a detour (the driver reports only that his navigation display refreshed and he continued), the fare_breakdown's erp_gantries array is empty so no charged gantry places the vehicle on a corridor the optimal route does not use, the driver's counterparty_statement denies the detour rather than admitting the route, and fare_breakdown.distance_charged_km (15.0 km) is a copy of the trace figure rather than an independent derivation. POL-RD-07(iii) therefore applies and the outcome is ESCALATE under POL-RD-10(3), which holds the disputed SGD 5.80 rather than collecting it.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason": "Cites the impaired artifact EV-GPS-09115 (weight_multiplier 0.6, issue code GPS_GAP) without disclosing the impairment or naming the issue code, as POL-GEN-02(1) requires; discarded on that ground."
    },
    {
      "claim": "The rider's initial burden under POL-RD-08 is not aggravated: rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0 and rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, so the extra-corroboration condition for unsubstantiated repeat claimants is not triggered, and the artifacts describe the same trip with a matching identifier, TRP-09115, across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown.",
      "side": "RIDER",
      "reason": "Cites the impaired artifact EV-GPS-09115 (weight_multiplier 0.6, issue code GPS_GAP) without disclosing the impairment or naming the issue code, as POL-GEN-02(1) requires; discarded on that ground."
    }
  ]
}
